NAME:🎬 SIFF (Uptown House 3)
X-WR-CALNAME:🎬 SIFF (Uptown House 3)
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:It’s Never Over\, Jeff Buckley
DTSTART:20250813T233000Z
DTEND:20250814T014000Z
DTSTAMP:20250813T233000Z
UID:cSnRYutmSv
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 106 mins (1h46m)\n\nThe definitive tale of Jeff Buck
 ley\, the rising young star with an otherworldly voice whose sudden death 
 at age 30\, after the release of his critically acclaimed debut album "Gra
 ce\," shocked the world. Told through never-before-seen footage from Buckl
 ey’s archives and intimate accounts. Exclusive 11"x17" poster for first 
 50 people in the door for the 7:30pm screening on Friday\, August 8! These
  exclusive pieces were designed by legendary rock 'n' roll illustrator Jes
 s Rotter\, are available exclusively in theaters\, and will not be printed
  again. Includes 26 minutes of exclusive\, remastered footage from a previ
 ously unreleased solo performance* filmed February 19\, 1994\, screening i
 mmediately after the film.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/its-
 never-over-jeff-buckley
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Together
DTSTART:20250814T024500Z
DTEND:20250814T045000Z
DTSTAMP:20250814T024500Z
UID:DSLEZ2jen5
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 102 mins (1h42m)\n\nYears into their relationship\, 
 Tim and Millie (Dave Franco and Alison Brie) find themselves at a crossroa
 ds as they move to the country\, abandoning all that is familiar in their 
 lives except each other. With tensions already flaring\, a nightmarish enc
 ounter with a mysterious\, unnatural force threatens to corrupt their live
 s\, their love\, and their flesh. Note: No Open Captions on July 29. "[A] 
 delightfully unhinged spin on the body horror joint."—Kate Erbland\, In
 dieWire\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/together
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sorry\, Baby
DTSTART:20250815T000000Z
DTEND:20250815T020500Z
DTSTAMP:20250815T000000Z
UID:HM74ephkpR
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 104 mins (1h44m)\n\nEva Victor (“Billions”) writ
 es\, directs\, and stars in this nonlinear\, seriocomic story about a mela
 ncholic English professor’s complicated path toward healing in the after
 math of an all-to-common tragedy. Winner of the Sundance 2025 Waldo Salt S
 creenwriting Award.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/sorry-baby
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
